  "question": {
    "text": "Compound A reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></math> and forms a compound B. Compound B reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> and excess of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;to form compound C which on passing through or reaction with saturated NaCl&nbsp;solution forms sodium hydrogen carbonate. Compound A. B and C, are respectively.",
